    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac6a20ad_6444ff91",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkIdentity.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 417,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T06:21:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently NetworkStatsService use NetworkIdentity to index usages per network.\nThat is to say, the NetworkStatsService does not support multiple transports per network yet.\nThis needs medium/large change to migrade to use transports and is listed in feature planning.\nDoes this work for you?",
      "parentUuid": "a249b780_3b9dafbb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 417,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 417,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "857861201b11f7e4e6a991b768406d3b85b89e71",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "526eba25_fbe0c339",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkIdentity.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 421,
      "author": {
        "id": 1304263
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-26T02:59:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if it\u0027s a good idea to reuse it. SubscriberId is set twice in this method. People who try to update or read the code may not be able to understand why subscriber Id was used instead of wifi network key(they\u0027re both unrelated fields.) Why do you not store it in a new field that is more appropriate for it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 420,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 421,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "857861201b11f7e4e6a991b768406d3b85b89e71",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e4345c5_abe50e1d",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkIdentity.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 421,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T06:21:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discuss with Jean.\nIt might be an overkill to create a new field just for testing.\nAlso, wifiNetworkKey is named for wifi. So we keep current plan, which is\nnot great but we can modify it later if we think it is necessary.\nDoes that work for you?",
      "parentUuid": "526eba25_fbe0c339",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 420,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 421,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "857861201b11f7e4e6a991b768406d3b85b89e71",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4fa7c02_814e11f6",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkIdentity.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 421,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-09T07:42:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Making new fields in network stats is tremendously expensive (performance and disk-space wise as well as amount of work), so making a new field is not really realistic.\n\nHowever I agree that the wifi key is probably a better choice than the subscriber ID. Yes it says \"wifi\", but this is a \"key\" and not at all a \"subscriber\". I think the identity of the field matters more than what it is applicable to.",
      "parentUuid": "526eba25_fbe0c339",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 420,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 421,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "857861201b11f7e4e6a991b768406d3b85b89e71",
